```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);
```

This statement checks if the new array list has a size at most as much as the old array list. If the condition is not met, an exception will be thrown.
--------------------Here are the output assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@":

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);
```
This assert statement checks whether the new size of the array list is less than or equal to the old size of the array list, effectively verifying that the "Remove" operation has not made the size of the array list larger.
--------------------```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);

// @@@ for a value in list, index of contains returns it 

Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= 0 && Old_arrListIndexOfX < New_arrListCount);

// @@@ for a value in list, last index of returns it 

Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= 0 && Old_arrListLastIndexOfX < New_arrListCount);

// @@@ for a value in list, contains returns true 

Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == false);

// @@@ for a value removed from the list, index of contains returns -1 

Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == -1);

// @@@ for a value removed from the list, last index of contains returns -1

Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1);
